---
# cert-err33-c lives here rather than in the repository root because this project publishes its output by a rename: a
# write error the file system held back has to be noticed before that rename runs. PasswordManager makes the same
# promise and keeps its own copy of this config. The root config is shared with projects that make no such promise and
# would only inherit the suppressions.

InheritParentConfig: true

Checks: >
  cert-err33-c

WarningsAsErrors: >
  cert-err33-c
